Source code for the pocket-ui @VERSION@ SD card image (Retroid Pocket Mini V2)
==========================================================================

Much of the software on this card is free software under the GNU General Public License (GPL) or the
GNU Lesser General Public License (LGPL): the Linux kernel, GRUB, BusyBox, the GNU C library, RetroArch,
many emulators, pocket-ui itself and more. You may have their complete source code.


Where it is
-----------

Next to this image, on @RELEASE_URL@ :

  pocket-ui-@VERSION@-source.tar.gz
      pocket-ui, pocket-core and pocket-splash, and the scripts that build this image
      (scripts/make-image.sh, scripts/image/, deploy/).

The rest of the source is public, at the exact versions on this card:
  ROCKNIX:    https://github.com/ROCKNIX/distribution/tree/@ROCKNIX_TAG@
              tag @ROCKNIX_TAG@, commit @ROCKNIX_COMMIT@. Every package's recipe (where its source
              comes from), the kernel configuration, all patches, and the scripts that put SYSTEM
              and KERNEL together ("make docker-SM8250" builds them).
  GRUB:       @GRUB_SOURCE_URL@
  ReGBA BIOS: https://github.com/Nebuleon/ReGBA/tree/7f379052dc14366e622a96c7cf7fb6b5a7e918a3/bios (GPL version 2 or later)
  pocket-ui:  @POCKET_UI_SOURCE@


Written offer
-------------

For at least three years from the release of this image, anyone can get the complete corresponding
source code of the GPL- and LGPL-licensed software on this card, for no charge beyond the cost of
providing it. To ask, open an issue titled "Source request" at @ISSUES_URL@ and name this image:
pocket-ui @VERSION@, pocket-ui-@VERSION@-rp-mini-v2.img.xz.
This offer is valid for anyone who has this information.
